ontent": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le09ob02re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le09ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le09ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le09ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "\u201cIt makes you money, doesn't it?\u201d \u201cNo? Then, It makes you happy, doesn't it?\u201d \u201cNo! Then why are you doing it?\u201d\n<br/>\nThat was my uncle Adam's opinion on my previous position. I liked to say if there hadn't been a strike, I would have stayed, or if management hadn't hired scab employees, I wouldn't have left.", "id": 1}, {"time": "23000", "image": "engenn9le09ob02re2img02.jpg", "text": "Deep down though, I knew if they had paid me more, I'd still be there and I wouldn't have quit if I had loved the job even a tiny bit more. His philosophy on work boils down to two questions: does it make you money, or does it make you happy? Which is fine, if you want to just pay your bills. But, to get my dream job, I need to dig a little deeper, don't I?  So, I came up with a couple more questions to help me.<br/>\nThe first one is, \u201cWhat big problem is driving me crazy right now?\u201d Solving this problem is the secret to helping me understand what I was born to do. For example, the education system is obsolete and there is opportunity in online learning, isn't there?  This leads me to the next question which is: \u201cWhat companies are solving my problem?\u201d", "id": 2}, {"time": "71000", "image": "engenn9le09ob02re2img03.jpg", "text": "If you had had something in common with that company then, it would have piqued your interest and your passion to work there. You now know a place that may hold your dream job. Now, you just need to find away to get your foot in the door and show them how eager you are to work there.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Job You Want"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "We All Have to Pay Our Bills"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If there <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hadn't been</span> a strike, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have stayed</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If management hadn't hired scab employees, I wouldn't have left. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Deep down though, I knew if they had paid me more, I'd still be there."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would not have quit if I loved the job even a tiny bit more."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use tag questions to ask for clarification and confirmation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Question tags are short questions at the end of statements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They are mainly used in speech when we want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm whether something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a reply</span> from the person we are speaking to.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">A <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">positive</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying \u2018no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "\u201cIt makes you money, doesn't it?\u201d"}, {"type": "example", "content": " \u201cNo? Then, It makes you happy, doesn't it?\u201d"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to dig a little deeper, don't I?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is opportunity in online learning, isn't there?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talk about a funny job hunting experience story, make one up or talk about a friend's or family member's experience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down what happened in point form."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, rewrite the story using hypothetical situations in the past focusing on the things you could have done differently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange stories with a partner and check each other's grammar."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change partners and read your story."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about a funny experience looking for a job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use hypothetical situations in the past to retell the story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I edit my partner's story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my story about a funny experiences looking for a job with others."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "boils down to"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to reduce to its essential"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: His philosophy on work boils down to two questions: does it make you money, or does it make you happy?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when making a job hunting strategy."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drives me crazy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "exasperate someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What a big problem, it's driving me crazy right now?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get your foot in the door"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to enter a business at a low level and take the opportunity to  be successful "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You just need to find away to get your foot in the door and show them how eager you are to work there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "piqued my interest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to arouse interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It would have piqued your interest and your passion to work there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deep down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "you are certain that is true"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Deep down though, I knew if they had paid me more, I'd still be there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "obsolete"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "no longer in general use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The education system is obsolete and there is opportunity in online learning, isn't there?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eager"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "show interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You just need to find away to get your foot in the door and show them how eager you are to work there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le09ob02re1img01.jpg"}]}